# ============================================================================
# Cloudflare Pages — redirect rules
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Parsed by Cloudflare Pages; NOT served as a static asset.
#
# Syntax:  <from>  <to>  [status]
#   · one rule per line, max 2100 rules
#   · splats (*) and :placeholders are supported
#   · default status is 302; use 301 for permanent moves
#   · rules are evaluated top to bottom, first match wins
#   · static files always win over redirects, so these only fire for paths
#     that do not exist on disk
# ============================================================================

# --- legacy case-study URLs -------------------------------------------------
# Case studies moved from project.html?id=<x> to /work/<x>/ so each one has a
# real, indexable URL with its own title and share card. project.html itself
# still exists as a JS redirect (it needs to read the ?id= query string, which
# Pages redirects cannot match on), so this is only a safety net for anyone who
# hand-trims the query.
/project                 /index.html#projects            301

# --- convenience aliases ----------------------------------------------------
# Short paths that are easy to say out loud in an interview or type from a
# business card.
/cv                      /resume.html                    301
/work                    /index.html#projects            301
/projects                /index.html#projects            301
/contact                 /index.html#contact             301
/experience              /index.html#experience          301
/games                   /index.html#games               301

# --- retired GitHub Pages paths ---------------------------------------------
# If anything was shared while the site was on github.io, keep it working.
/index                   /                               301